DNS
1. what it is
- domain name service
- a system to translate domain names to ip addresses
- ip addresses are octets (series of 8 numbers)
2. ip addresses
- classless ip addresses: 0.0.0.0 to 255.255.255.255 ( 0 to (28)4) -> too small number
-> public and private ips
- public ips are ips that everyone can see 
- private ips are ips that only devices in the same network can see
Hst17.com        97.74.93.87     01100001. 01001010. 01011101. 01010111
->>>>> translation : done by DNS

3. layers of DNS
- local machine
- router
- isp (internet service provider: vnpt, fpt, Viettel…) - google dns
- regional dns
- root dns

**all the ip translations are kept by the dns records stored in each level

ipconfig /flushdns
